<!--
    kuna issue testcase: no AIF gap entry starts on nop padding
    (`option aifnoppad on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants entries that are not function starts
                on large i386 PEs; most of the non-start ones are the nop runs
                in front of Wine's relay thunks.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the AIF gap-walk probe
                (`analyzers/aif/kuna_aifnoppad.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option aifnoppad on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `aifnoppad_pe_i386.exe` (source `aifnoppad_pe_i386.asm`
    beside it): five called stubs open with nine nops, so `nop, nop` is a
    shared prologue fingerprint; eight nops pad from `relay`'s `ret 4` to the
    called `hot` at 0x401230; `dead` at 0x401239 opens with `mov edi,edi`
    straight after a return; `lone` at 0x40124c sits behind six nops with a
    prologue nothing else shares.  Neither `dead` nor `lone` is referenced.

    Pass 1 (`mode aggressive`, `option aifnoppad off`) reproduces the bug:
    the inventory lists sub_401228 and sub_401248, both on nops.
    Pass 2 (`mode aggressive`, shipped default) drops both, lists `lone` at
    its own address, and keeps `dead`: `mov edi,edi` is not padding.
    Pass 3 (`mode aggressive`, `option aif off`) shows `dead` and `lone` are
    the gap walk's own finds.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
